;
UPLOADS AND LIBRARY MAINTENANCE

A - Trying a transfer
B - Reviewing submissions
:A
TRYING A TRANSFER

Try transfers yourself before helping callers with them.
YSEND A0:WELCOME.TXT sends a file using YMODEM.
UPLOAD FILE.EXT accepts an XMODEM/CRC upload.
UPLOAD /Y accepts a YMODEM batch.

Start the matching operation in the terminal program when prompted.
Uploads go into the private host inbox, not the public library or
the caller's WORK directory.
:B
REVIEWING SUBMISSIONS

Look in uploads/inbox/ on the host for completed submissions.
Check the integrity and contents of archives, retain author notices,
and confirm redistribution is permitted before adding files to a
public collection.

Prepare or edit images while the system is stopped, using the
matching disk format. Keep backups of images before changing them.
Do not approve uploaded executables simply because they arrived
from a registered caller. See HELP AUTH and HELP DISKS.
